<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Grand Duchy of Frankfurt</h1><p class="st-meta">1810 CE – 1813 CE · capital Frankfurt am Main</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleonic grand duchy centred on Frankfurt, created for Karl Theodor von Dalberg and destined for Napoleon's stepson.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1810 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-theodor-von-dalberg">Dalberg</a> ceded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-regensburg">Regensburg</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and in exchange received <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hanau-munzenberg">Hanau</a> and Fulda. These were combined with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschaffenburg">Aschaffenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-wetzlar">Wetzlar</a> to form the Grand Duchy of Frankfurt, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> stepson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugene-de-beauharnais">Eugène de Beauharnais</a> named as Dalberg's successor.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The grand duchy was divided into four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> on the French model. A constitution of 1810 introduced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a> and equal rights, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> bought their civic equality in 1811. Frankfurt remained a major trading and banking centre, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a> hurt trade and the state had to provide troops for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karl-theodor-von-dalberg">Dalberg</a> abdicated in October 1813, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugene-de-beauharnais">Eugène</a> never succeeded. The allies placed it under provisional administration; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> became a free city, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hanau-munzenberg">Hanau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulda">Fulda</a> went to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hesse">Electorate of Hesse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aschaffenburg">Aschaffenburg</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grand-duchy-of-frankfurt.jpg" alt="Grand Duchy of Frankfurt" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan, wheel from File:Coat of Arms of Ernest August, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg (1661-1692).svg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Electorate_of_Mainz.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1810 CE – 1813 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Frankfurt am Main</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Karl Theodor von Dalberg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Großherzogtum Frankfurt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1812&amp;focus=grand-duchy-of-frankfurt" aria-label="Grand Duchy of Frankfurt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4879 435 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Grand Duchy of Frankfurt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5199 691L5279 723M5199 691L5199 691M5199 691L5199 691M5199 691L5210 695"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5279 723h0M5199 691h0M5199 691h0M5210 695h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5199 691h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5199 691h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1812&amp;focus=grand-duchy-of-frankfurt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
